.TH PNPD 8 "September 2026" "pnpd 0.5.0" "Peios System Administration"
.SH NAME
pnpd \- observe and author Peios Network Policy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pnpd
.RB [ \-\-port " " N ]
.RB [ \-\-ring " " N ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pnpd
captures packets, consumes the Peios Network Policy verdict stream, and serves
the PNP viewer and policy-authoring interface over HTTP.
It is an observation and authoring service; policy enforcement remains in the
kernel.
.PP
The service currently belongs to the Experimental edition.
Its HTTP interface has no authentication boundary and must not be exposed to
an untrusted network.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-port " N"
Listen on TCP port
.IR N .
The default is 8081.
.TP
.BI \-\-ring " N"
Keep at most
.I N
captured packets in the in-memory history ring.
The default is 4096.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/peios-pnp
Kernel verdict stream and query interface.
.TP
.I Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules
Registry policy tree read and edited by the viewer.
.SH SECURITY
The current development service runs as SYSTEM, opens a raw packet socket,
listens on all addresses, and permits policy mutation through its HTTP
interface without authentication.
Keep TCP port 8081 unreachable from untrusted networks.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR netd (8)
